# Glyph Grid

## Unit system

```js
const u = (n) => `calc(${n} * var(--u))`;
// --u = --glyph-h / --glyph-units  (set in css/styles.css on .glyph-stage)
// --glyph-units = aboveH + mainH + belowH  (must stay in sync with glyph-layout.json)
```

All sizes/offsets in `glyph-layout.json` are **SVG slice units**. Apply via `u()`.

## Mask URLs — set inline, not via CSS custom property

CSS custom properties containing `url()` resolve relative to the **stylesheet**, not the document. Setting `mask` directly as an inline style resolves relative to the document (correct).

```js
// ✅ CORRECT — relative URL resolves against document
const maskVal = `url("${m.url}") no-repeat center / 100% 100%`;
el.style.webkitMask = maskVal;
el.style.mask = maskVal;

// ❌ WRONG — url() inside custom property resolves relative to css/styles.css
el.style.setProperty("--mask", `url("${m.url}")`);
```

## Shad dy — use u() like everything else

`cells.shad.dy` works with `u()` just like all other offsets. The old px-formula workaround was solving the wrong problem (the real bug was dy=0 in stale JSON, not var(--u) failing to resolve):

```js
// ✅ CORRECT — consistent with all other parts
marginTop: u(cells.shad.dy ?? 0),

// ❌ WRONG — hardcoded px formula, breaks if --glyph-h changes
marginTop: `${shadDy * (11 / 1020) * 16}px`
```

## Grid areas

Columns: `root | tsheg | shad` (tsheg/shad columns only exist when shown).  
Rows: `vowelAbove | main | vowelBelow`.

`.glyph-part--shad` → `grid-column: 3` only (not 2/4).

## perGlyph tweaks

In `glyph-layout.json → perGlyph.<wylie>`:
- `crossbarTop` — distance (units) from slice top to crossbar top. Root is shifted up by `crossbarTop * scale` so crossbar aligns with main row top.
- `dx` / `dy` — nudge root only.

**crossbarTop varies by consonant shape:**
- Rows 1–4 (ka/kha/ga/nga…): ~47 — no top extensions
- Row 5 (tsa/tsha/dza): flag on top-right corner extends above crossbar → larger value
- Rows 6–8: shapes vary; measure each

**Tuning workflow** (browser, no measurement needed):
1. Add `perGlyph.<wylie>: { crossbarTop: 0, scale: 1 }` to JSON
2. Load `?shad=1` — shad will be at the top of the main row
3. Adjust `scale` until letter matches the visual size of ka (slices have inconsistent bounding box heights)
4. Increase `crossbarTop` until shad top aligns with the crossbar stroke
5. Save values; move to next consonant

**Note:** Slice bounding boxes are inconsistent across consonants. `perGlyph.scale` compensates — ka = 1.0 reference. Letters sliced with a smaller box need scale > 1.

## Layout JSON reload

`glyph-layout.json` is a **static Vite import** — HMR does a full page reload on save. Changes are read once per page load. `npm run build` required to bake into `dist/`.
